<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afro-Shirazi Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1957">1957</a>–<a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as ASP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Afro-Shirazi Party was a Zanzibari political party formed in 1957 to represent the islands' African and Shirazi majority. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abeid-karume">Abeid Karume</a>, it came to power after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanzibar-revolution">Zanzibar Revolution</a> of January 1964 and ruled the People's Republic of Zanzibar as a single party. In 1977 it merged with the mainland's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanganyika-african-national-union">TANU</a> to form <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chama-cha-mapinduzi">Chama Cha Mapinduzi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/afro-shirazi-party.jpg" alt="Afro-Shirazi Party" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Own work · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Afro-Shirazi_party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
